.TH MEMORY-MAP 1 2026-10-12 "memory-map @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
memory-map \- show the computer's memory use as a live treemap
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B memory-map
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B memory-map
opens a window showing RAM as a treemap refreshed every second: apps in the
user's session, system services, virtual machines and containers, kernel
memory, shared memory and cache, and available memory.
Each process is sized by its private memory (RssAnon), which needs no root.
.PP
Tabs show the same items as a table, the last hour as a chart, and the
programs that start at login, each with a switch for this user only.
A tray icon and a low-memory alert are shown where the desktop has a tray.
.PP
Right-click a process to end it (always confirmed) or open its folder;
both work for the user's own processes only.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/MemoryMap/settings.json
Settings: refresh interval, alert threshold, close to tray.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/
Where switching a startup entry writes this user's copy.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR free (1),
.BR ps (1)
